## 18. API Contract Summary

Screen API base is normally `VITE_API_BASE`, defaulting to `http://localhost:8000/screen` in development.

Screen endpoints used by the dashboard:

- `GET /crypto-exchanges`
- `GET /stock-filter-options`
- `POST /run`
- `POST /run-gate`
- `POST /run-entry`
- `POST /details`

Backend root endpoints used by status/settings:

- `GET /`
- `GET /healthz`
- `GET /readyz`

Ops endpoints used by settings:

- `GET /ops/worker`
- worker mutation paths through the worker helper
- `GET /ops/runtime-settings`
- `GET /ops/integrations`
- `POST /ops/integrations/config`
- `GET /ops/integrations/{name}/history`
- `GET /ops/diagnose`

Request payloads are JSON and match `ScreenerRequest` or `ScreenerDetailRequest`.

## 19. Data Persistence

Firestore document:

- `users/{uid}`

Stored user data:

- API settings
- admin token
- timezone
- indicator defaults
- post-filter defaults
- saved presets
- watchlist
- disabled indicators
- worker settings

LocalStorage keys:

- `screener.apiBaseOverride`
- `screener.apiTimeoutMs`
- `screener.apiRetries`
- `screener.indicatorDefaults`
- `screener.postFilterDefaults`

